2186277021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278066 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278066 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278066 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278066 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278066 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186277021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278066 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c006b05b-e312-5e14-bc62-bb96f8a28156" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278231 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278231 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159585" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278231 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278231 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy,$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(0,\\pi ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278231 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e406b09c-bfce-50a6-b8a5-dd556a32ecbf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278231 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\pi  \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\pi -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278234 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278234 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159594" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278234 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278234 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278234 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53daed36-1f31-5b2b-8966-96a4d35c598d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278234 #edb/ref 1074 "The derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x,y+h)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x,y+h)=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-(y+h)}-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}-y}}{h}).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278236 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278236 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159599" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278236 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278236 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{x}^{7}y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,\\frac{1}{2}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278236 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d7d1dc5-2124-525b-9cc9-fe9b2cf1012d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278236 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{x}^{7}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{7}y) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+{x}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{y})+{x}^{7}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{y}+{x}^{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,\\frac{1}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1/2)} & =\\frac{{e}^{1}}{(\\frac{1}{2})}+{1}^{7} \\\\  & =2e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278241 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278241 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159619" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278241 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278241 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-8{y}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278241 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8fe04cdb-3f03-5a9d-a32d-3dd7d276f6a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278241 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation ${f}_{x}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-8{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-8{y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381181 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186381182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381181 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159587" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381181 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381181 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x,y)={y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(4,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381181 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83c38041-fc9b-546f-afa6-2d3c332d1b5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381181 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\sqrt{x}+x{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\sqrt{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (2y)+x\\cdot (-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2y\\sqrt{x}-x{y}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(4,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(4,2)} & =2\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{4}-4\\cdot {2}^{-2} \\\\  & =8-1 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186381186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381182 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7d6eafe7-491c-520d-9960-7135619c340c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381183 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381183 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381183 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2383a34d-6e32-5f0f-87b8-e7ec3d81fb75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381184 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{9}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381184 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381184 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f18943a3-6ebe-57f1-9bae-7fc754040e67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381185 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381185 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381185 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "062115ff-ad39-57f6-a416-c53bab27effc" #edb/ref 175921